  "body": "The context here is that we'd like to change our default logging to a) not take up so much room and b) use less disk I/O. For installations where we write logs to the disk we can do things like use buffered logging (#8018) and/or keeping INFO logging for a shorter period of time (#8019). Unfortunately, for docker Synapse logs to stderr which is then picked up by the docker daemon, making it hard/impossible to do the same sort of things we did when writing to disk.\r\n\r\nSome potential ideas:\r\n- Log WARN to stderr, INFO to a mounted volume\r\n- Investigate if we can fiddle with e.g. syslog to make it to the write thing and then document that, etc",
